--
--   **Context.** B-line axis program (`AxisU6`), part 1: the pass contracts and the chain
--
--   The axis program of `AxisBody6` is a sequence of passes, each in the convention of `FineBody6`
--   (only stack `0`, the descriptor stack `dA` and, for the two-array steps, `rZ = 53` are nonempty):
--
--       pass1 (slabSc) ; pass2 (chunk kernel) ; copy (Y → rZ) ; pass3 (gather) ; pass4 (J kernel) ;
--       pass5 (scatter) ; pass6 (chunk kernel) ; swap (0 ↔ rZ) ; pass7 (slabOut)
--
--   * `PassOK Isym tbl st dA desc Pre g C`: `st` maps the array `L` on stack `0` to `g L`
--     (precondition `Pre L`), reading `desc` on `dA`, cost `≤ C`.
--   * `Pass2OK Isym tbl st dA desc Pre g C`: the same for the pair (stack `0`, stack `rZ`):
--     `(A, B) ↦ g A B`. The copy is `g A [] = (A, A)`, the swap `g A B = (B, A)`, the output pass
--     `g Y Y₂ = (out, [])`.
--   * `axis_chain`: the nine steps compose (the copy of `Y` on `rZ` is carried through passes 3–6 in
--     the base state).
